# Line endings are a correctness concern here, not a style one.
#
# The blueprint library carries an integrity manifest of SHA-256 checksums over RAW BYTES
# (TASK-021, REQ-F-042). With Git's default autocrlf on Windows, the same blueprint is LF in
# the repository and CRLF in the working tree — so the same file would hash differently on
# Windows and Linux, and the control would fire on every clone while catching nothing.
#
# Pinning eol=lf means every checkout, on every platform, has identical bytes. That is what
# lets the checksum be over raw bytes rather than over content normalised at hash time —
# normalising inside the hasher would hide a real alteration behind an encoding change.
#
# REQ-NF-008 says behaviour must be identical on Windows, macOS, and Linux. For a payload
# whose checksums are a control, "identical" has to mean the bytes.

plugin/**                text eol=lf
spec-driven-template/**  text eol=lf

# Compared byte-for-byte against the packaged library by TEST-003; must convert identically.
spec-driven-devkit/**    text eol=lf

ci/**                    text eol=lf
tests/**                 text eol=lf

*.png binary
